  "extraction_notes": [
    "The supplied PDF SHA-256 matches 0b87e03cdc2b7ad711297d07ee72ee11a3c600476107c87e790de14f82884e63.",
    "The PDF identifies the device as a silicon PNP transistor in an SOT-23 package, with pin 1 = base, pin 2 = emitter, and pin 3 = collector. The requested MPN S8550M-D is the D hFE classification variant; p. 1 lists D marking HY4D and hFE range 160-300, while the p. 2 electrical table is headed for S8550M generally.",
    "All p. 2 electrical-characteristics values were transcribed with Ta = 25 degC and with the datasheet's negative PNP polarity. Minimum, typical, and maximum meanings are preserved in source_kind; no guaranteed bounds were converted to typical values.",
    "Curve points were digitized directly at labeled major or minor grid positions from p. 3. The PNP plots display positive magnitudes, so curve axes and conditions explicitly identify magnitudes; curve values are not signed terminal voltages or currents.",
    "The p. 2 table gives VBE typ = -0.66 V and max = -1.0 V at VCE = -1.0 V and IC = -10 mA; the strict schema has no dedicated VBE(on) field, so this permitted table fact is recorded here rather than omitted silently.",
    "The p. 2 table gives fT minimum = 100 MHz and typical = 200 MHz at VCE = -10 V and IC = -50 mA; ft stores the guaranteed minimum and the typical value is preserved here because the strict schema has only one ft object.",
    "The p. 2 table gives VCBO minimum = -40 V at IC = -0.1 mA, IE = 0; VEBO minimum = -6.0 V at IE = -0.1 mA, IC = 0; ICBO maximum = -0.1 uA at VCB = -35 V, IE = 0; and IEBO maximum = -0.1 uA at VEB = -6.0 V, IC = 0. These have no dedicated fields in the strict schema.",
    "The p. 3 PC-Ta derating plot is included as drawn. Its approximately 450 mW value at Ta = 25 degC conflicts with the p. 2 absolute-maximum PC rating of 200 mW; the table rating should not be replaced by the plotted curve.",
    "No cibo/input-capacitance value is published in the supplied datasheet, so cibo is null."
  ],
